# Drafted by Gemini (R11 batch b3), edited. holly_aster's first conversation.

~ start
set holly_aster_met
Narrator: Warm cinnamon and browned butter pour from the bakehouse door. Holly wipes flour from her apron with quick, restless fingers, her cheeks flushed red from the brick ovens.
holly_aster [smile]: Fresh loaves, honey cakes, and plum tarts, hot off the peel! Come in before the chill gets into the crust.
-> menu

~ menu
holly_aster [smile]: The ovens stay hot till Nightfall strikes. What can I wrap up for you?
* Browse their wares -> shop_open
* Ask about her baking and her family -> work
* Ask about the Old Ways and the village -> village
* Ask about the bells and the hours -> rumour
* [Perception DC 14] Notice her trembling hands and whispered counting -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ shop_open
holly_aster [smile]: Sweet rye, seeded rolls, and spiced buns, take plenty for the road!
shop
-> menu

~ work
holly_aster [smile]: Violet braids the dough-rings now, and little Lavender puts the cloves in the tarts. Siv keeps the hearth stacked and the house steady when my head gets spinning.
-> menu

~ village
holly_aster [neutral]: I leave the first loaf of every batch at the roots of the Oak for the Green Queen. The Old Ways kept this village fed long before we got here, and I won't have my girls forgetting their manners.
-> menu

~ rumour
holly_aster [weary]: The two grand folk from the estate rode past at early Twilight in their fine coat-cloth. When lords come down to the moor, it's always the village that pays the reckoning.
-> menu

~ secret_ok
Narrator: Flour sifts from her shaking knuckles as she taps the kneading board in sets of seven, her lips moving without sound whenever the clocktower creaks.
holly_aster [afraid]: Thirty-four loaves on the rack, and never room for one more. If a woman owes a debt she didn't sign for, all the prayers to the Oak won't stop the house from calling her number.
-> menu

~ secret_fail
holly_aster [smile]: Just counting the seconds on the ginger-crust, strangers, a baker who loses count burns the batch!
-> menu
